[38;2;124;124;124mHmm, let me reconsider. The number of closed subsets of R: A closed set F is the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mcomplement of an open set. An open set in R is a countable union of disjoint [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mopen intervals, each determined by its endpoints (which are real numbers or ±∞).[0m[38;2;124;124;124mSo an open set is determined by a countable sequence of pairs of reals. The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnumber of such sequences is c^ℵ₀ = c. So the number of open sets is at most c, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mand the number of closed sets is at most c.[0m

